0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-23).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Four switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a three-line report: the letter and the place as
0000                             ;                 line and column, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     1 = the four console codes (`@ `^ `_ `?) send ANSI escape
0000                             ;                 sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = they call four routines of the machine's own instead:
0000                             ;                 CONAT, CONCLS, CONEOL and CONCUR (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   0   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console codes send ANSI sequences
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-ANSI)   
                                 ; ---- generic machine with ANSI = 0: the console codes call these ------------
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF0Ch   ; `@  cursor to row E, column L, both from 0
                                 ;     (DE and HL hold the whole cells). May
                                 ;     change A, DE and HL
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; `^  clear the screen and home the cursor
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF12h   ; `_  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF15h   ; `?  cursor off if A = 0 (the zero flag is set
                                 ;     to match), on if not. May change A, DE, HL
                                 ;   All four must preserve BC and HL'; CONCLS and CONEOL also DE and HL.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
                    EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
                    SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0000                SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                SEED:     EQU   LET+76h   ; gap after z: the random seed, the cell whose
0000                             ;   address `. gives. Nothing sets it at the
0000                             ;   start but the checked build's clearing;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ;   a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0100                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0100                          IF   1-EDGEN   
0100   31 FC 08               LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   EDGEN   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
                              LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
                              JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
                              NOP      ; 07  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   CPM   
0103   C3 47 06               JP   start   ; 03
0106   00 00                  DW   0   ; 06  spare
0108                          ENDIF      
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0108   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0109   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
010A   23                     INC   HL   
010B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
010C   23                     INC   HL   
010D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
010E   D9                     EXX      
010F   D1                     POP   DE   
0110   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0111                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0111   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0113   20 1F                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0115   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0118                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   18 15                  JR   nx   
011C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
011D   CF                     RST   08h   
011E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
011F   F7                     RST   30h   
0120                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     LD   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     LD   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0128                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 F2 04               JP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
012C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
012D   C3 C9 01               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0130                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                NX:          
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
0134   CD 0B 05               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0137                          ENDIF      
0137   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0138   03                     INC   BC   
0139   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013B   38 D4                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013D   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
013F   38 25                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0141   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0143   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0145   38 6C                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0147   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0149   38 19                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
014B   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
014D   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
014F   38 6E                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0151   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0153   38 0D                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0155   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0157   38 60                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0159   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
015B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
015B                          ENDIF      
015B                          IF   CHECKED   
015B   28 D7                  JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
015D   D2 37 05               JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0160                          ENDIF      
0160   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0162   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0164   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0166                .macro PTABLE,
0166                             ; 
0166                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0166                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0166                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0166                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0166                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0166                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0166                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0166                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0166                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0166                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0166                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0166                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0166                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0166                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0166                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0166                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0166                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0166                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0166                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0166                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0166                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0166                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0166                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0166                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0166                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0166                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0166                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0166                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0166                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0166                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0166                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0166                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0166                .endm
0166                 
0166                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0166                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0166   C6 80        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0168   5F                     LD   E,A   
0169   16 04                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
016B   FE 96                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
016D   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
016E   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
016F                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
016F                          ENDIF      
016F                          IFN   CPM   
                              RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
016F                          ENDIF      
016F                          IF   CPM   
016F   16 01                  LD   D,1   
0171   30 01                  JR   NC,pu1   
0173   14                     INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
0174                PU1:         
0174                          ENDIF      
0174   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0175   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0176                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0176                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0176                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0176                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0176                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0176                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0176                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0176   22 7C 09     ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0179                          ENDIF      
0179                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
0179   E7                     RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
017A   22 38 09               LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
017D                          ENDIF      ;   these)
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
                              LD   HL,0   
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   1-EDITOR   
017D   D9                     EXX      
017E   21 E0 07               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
0181   D9                     EXX      
0182   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0183                          ENDIF      
0183                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0183                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0183                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0183                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0183                          ENDIF      
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0183                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0183                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0184   7C                     LD   A,H   
0185   AA                     XOR   D   
0186   67                     LD   H,A   
0187   7D                     LD   A,L   
0188   AB                     XOR   E   
0189   6F                     LD   L,A   
018A   F7                     RST   30h   
018B   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
018C   7C                     LD   A,H   
018D   B2                     OR   D   
018E   67                     LD   H,A   
018F   7D                     LD   A,L   
0190   B3                     OR   E   
0191   6F                     LD   L,A   
0192   F7                     RST   30h   
0193   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0194   2B                     DEC   HL   
0195   F7                     RST   30h   
0196                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0196                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0196   ED 5B 7C 09  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
019A                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
019A   7C                     LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
019B                          ENDIF      
019B   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
019C                          IF   CHECKED   
019C   CD 41 05               CALL   chkhp   
019F                          ENDIF      
019F   22 7C 09               LD   (HEAP),HL   
01A2   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
01A3   F7                     RST   30h   
01A4   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
01A5   22 34 09               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
01A8   D9                     EXX      
01A9   CD 2B 01               CALL   jphl   
01AC   D9                     EXX      
01AD   2A 34 09               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
01B0   D9                     EXX      
01B1   E1                     POP   HL   
01B2   F7                     RST   30h   
01B3                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
01B3                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
01B3                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
01B3   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
01B4   0B                     DEC   BC   
01B5   CD 37 03               CALL   rdnum   
01B8   F7                     RST   30h   
01B9                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01B9   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
01BA   87                     ADD   A,A   
01BB   6F                     LD   L,A   
01BC   26 09                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
01BE   F7                     RST   30h   
01BF                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01BF                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01BF   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
01C0   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
01C1   87                     ADD   A,A   
01C2   6F                     LD   L,A   
01C3   26 09                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01C5   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
01C6   2C                     INC   L   
01C7   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
01C8   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
01C9                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
01C9                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
01C9                             ; 
01C9                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01C9                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
01C9                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
01C9                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
01C9                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
01C9                             ; both ways out.)
01C9   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
01CA   D1                     POP   DE   
01CB   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CC   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01CD   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CE   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01CF   05                     DEC   B   
01D0   D9                     EXX      
01D1   CC B2 04               CALL   Z,pollk   
01D4   F7                     RST   30h   
01D5                             ; ---- the grave -------------------------------------------------------------
01D5                             ; The grave is a prefix: with the character after it, it is one command.
01D5                             ; The characters are tested one after another, each SUB taking off the step
01D5                             ; from the one before, so A is 0 (and the carry clear) when a handler is
01D5                             ; reached. Two are here, where they keep the first page as full as the
01D5                             ; layout needs; grave2 has the rest.
01D5                             ; 
01D5                             ;   `!  ( addr -- )  calls the machine code at TOS. The code is entered by
01D5                             ;       CALL with the data stack above the return address; it must keep BC,
01D5                             ;       and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01D5                             ;   `'  ( -- )  new line: CR LF
01D5   0A           H_GRAVE:   LD   A,(BC)   
01D6   03                     INC   BC   
01D7   D6 21                  SUB   "!"   
01D9   28 C9                  JR   Z,exec   
01DB   D6 06                  SUB   27h-"!"   ; "'"
01DD   C2 B5 03               JP   NZ,grave2   
01E0   3E 0D                  LD   A,13   
01E2   EF                     RST   28h   
01E3   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
01E5   EF                     RST   28h   
01E6   F7                     RST   30h   
01E7                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01E7                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01E7                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01E7                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01E7                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01E7                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
01E7   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
01E8   42                     LD   B,D   
01E9   4B                     LD   C,E   
01EA   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
01EB                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01EB                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01EB   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
01EC   B5                     OR   L   
01ED   E1                     POP   HL   
01EE   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
01F0   CD 5E 03               CALL   skip   
01F3   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01F4   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
01F6   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
01F7   F7                     RST   30h   
01F8                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01F8                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01F8                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01F8                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01F8                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01F8   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
01F9   03                     INC   BC   
01FA   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01FC   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01FD   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
01FF   FE 1A                  CP   26   
0201   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
0203   CB 23                  SLA   E   
0205   16 09                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0207   79                     LD   A,C   
0208   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0209   1C                     INC   E   
020A   78                     LD   A,B   
020B   12                     LD   (DE),A   
020C   18 09                  JR   skipnx   
020E                DEF2:        
020E                          IF   CHECKED   
020E   7B                     LD   A,E   
020F   FE DF                  CP   " "-"A"+256   
0211   C2 82 05               JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0214                          ENDIF      
0214   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0215   60                     LD   H,B   
0216   69                     LD   L,C   
0217                SKIPNX:      
0217                          IF   CHECKED   
0217   0B                     DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
0218                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
0218   CD 5E 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
021B   F7                     RST   30h   
021C   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
021D   23                     INC   HL   
021E   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
021F   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0220   F7                     RST   30h   
0221                             ; =============================================================================
0221                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0221                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0221                             ;  page.
0221                             ; =============================================================================
0221                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0221                             ; the matching ")".
0221   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0222   B5                     OR   L   
0223   E1                     POP   HL   
0224   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
0226   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
0227   18 A0                  JR   rpushn   
0229                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
0229                             ; drops it and carries on.
0229   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
022A   B5                     OR   L   
022B   E1                     POP   HL   
022C   28 C8                  JR   Z,rdrop   
022E   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
022F   42                     LD   B,D   
0230   4B                     LD   C,E   
0231   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0232   18 95                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0234                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0234                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0234   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0235   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0237   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0239   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
023B   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
023C   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
023D   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
023E   F7                     RST   30h   
023F   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0240   CD 37 03               CALL   rdnum   
0243   E7                     RST   20h   
0244   F7                     RST   30h   
0245   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
0246   7C                     LD   A,H   
0247   A2                     AND   D   
0248   67                     LD   H,A   
0249   7D                     LD   A,L   
024A   A3                     AND   E   
024B   6F                     LD   L,A   
024C   F7                     RST   30h   
024D                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
024D                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
024D                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
024D                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
024D   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
024E   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
024F   7C                     LD   A,H   
0250   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0252   67                     LD   H,A   
0253   7A                     LD   A,D   
0254   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0256   57                     LD   D,A   
0257   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
0259   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
025B   F7                     RST   30h   
025C   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
025D   B7                     OR   A   
025E   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0260   7C                     LD   A,H   
0261   B5                     OR   L   
0262   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0264   18 F3                  JR   tf   
0266                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
0266                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
0266   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
0267   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0268   7C                     LD   A,H   
0269   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
026A   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
026D   06 10                  LD   B,16   
026F   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0270   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0272   17                     RLA      
0273   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0275   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0276   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
0278   C1                     POP   BC   
0279   F7                     RST   30h   
027A                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
027A                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
027A                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
027A                             ; stops on it.
027A                H_DIV:       
027A                          IF   CHECKED   
027A   7C                     LD   A,H   
027B   B5                     OR   L   
027C   CA 7F 05               JP   Z,e_zero   
027F                          ENDIF      
027F   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0280   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
0281   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0282   7A                     LD   A,D   
0283   AC                     XOR   H   
0284   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0285   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0287   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
028A   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
028B   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
028D   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0290   CD 11 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0293   F1                     POP   AF   
0294   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0297   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
0298   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
0299   B7                     OR   A   
029A   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
029D   C1                     POP   BC   
029E   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
029F   F7                     RST   30h   
02A0                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02A0   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
02A1   F7                     RST   30h   
02A2   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
02A3   F7                     RST   30h   
02A4                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
02A4                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
02A4                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
02A4                          IF   CHECKED   
02A4   CD 5E 05               CALL   chkst   
02A7                          ENDIF      
02A7   D1                     POP   DE   
02A8   73                     LD   (HL),E   
02A9   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
02AA                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02AA                          IF   CHECKED   
02AA   CD 5E 05               CALL   chkst   
02AD                          ENDIF      
02AD   D1                     POP   DE   
02AE   73                     LD   (HL),E   
02AF   23                     INC   HL   
02B0   72                     LD   (HL),D   
02B1   DF                     RST   18h   
02B2                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02B2                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02B2   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
02B3   60                     LD   H,B   
02B4   69                     LD   L,C   
02B5   CD 4D 03               CALL   skipstr   
02B8                          IF   CHECKED   
02B8   B7                     OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
02B9   CA 77 05               JP   Z,e_quote   
02BC                          ENDIF      
02BC   F7                     RST   30h   
02BD                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
02BD                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
02BD                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
02BD                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
02BD                          ENDIF      
02BD                          IF   CHECKED   
02BD                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
02BD                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
02BD                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
02BD   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
02BE   CD 27 06               CALL   prstr   
02C1   D1                     POP   DE   
02C2   DF                     RST   18h   
02C3                          ENDIF      
02C3   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
02C4   EF                     RST   28h   
02C5   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
02C6                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02C6   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
02C7   CD 9B 03               CALL   psgn   
02CA   C1                     POP   BC   
02CB   DF                     RST   18h   
02CC                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02CC                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02CC                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02CC                             ;          (both stir the random seed while they wait: see kt2)
02CC                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02CC                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02CC   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
02CE   20 22                  JR   NZ,line   
02D0   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02D2   CD E0 04     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02D5   20 17                  JR   NZ,kt3   
02D7   1D                     DEC   E   
02D8   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
02DA   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; a millisecond with no key stirs the random
02DB   2A 76 09               LD   HL,(SEED)   ;   seed by one: how long a key takes to come
02DE   23                     INC   HL   ;   is the one thing here that is not the
02DF   22 76 09               LD   (SEED),HL   ;   same every time
02E2   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
02E3   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02E4   B5                     OR   L   
02E5   28 E9                  JR   Z,kt1   
02E7   2B                     DEC   HL   
02E8   7C                     LD   A,H   
02E9   B5                     OR   L   
02EA   20 E4                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02EC   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
02ED   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02EE   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
02EF   26 00                  LD   H,0   
02F1   F7                     RST   30h   
02F2                          IF   CPM   
02F2                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
02F2                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
02F2   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
02F5   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
02F6   9F                     SBC   A,A   
02F7   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
02F8   EE 7F                  XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
02FA   32 7E 09               LD   (LBHDR),A   
02FD   11 7E 09               LD   DE,LBHDR   
0300   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0302   CD FE 04               CALL   bdosx   
0305   21 7F 09               LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
0308   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
0309   2C                     INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
030A   85                     ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
030B   6F                     LD   L,A   
030C   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
030E                          ENDIF      
030E                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CPL      
                              LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JR   Z,ln2   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ln5   
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,ln4   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ln2   ; full
                              LD   (HL),E   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
030E                          ENDIF      
030E   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0310   F7                     RST   30h   
0311                             ; =============================================================================
0311                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
0311                             ; =============================================================================
0311                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
0311                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
0311                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
0311                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0311   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
0312   EE 02                  XOR   2   
0314   B2                     OR   D   
0315   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
0317   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
0319   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
031B   8F                     ADC   A,A   
031C   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
031D   C9                     RET      
031E   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
031F   4D                     LD   C,L   
0320   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0323   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0325   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
0327   17                     RLA      
0328   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
032A   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
032C   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
032E   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
032F   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
0330   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
0331   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
0333   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
0334   67                     LD   H,A   
0335   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
0336   C9                     RET      
0337                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0337                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0337   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
033A   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
033B   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
033D   FE 0A                  CP   10   
033F   D0                     RET   NC   
0340   03                     INC   BC   
0341   54                     LD   D,H   
0342   5D                     LD   E,L   
0343   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0344   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0345   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0346   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
0347   5F                     LD   E,A   
0348   16 00                  LD   D,0   
034A   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
034B   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
034D                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
034D                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
034D                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INC   BC   
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   Z,ss0   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              RET      
034D                          ENDIF      
034D                          IF   CHECKED   
034D                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
034D                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
034D   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
034E   B7                     OR   A   
034F   C8                     RET   Z   
0350   03                     INC   BC   
0351   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0353   C8                     RET   Z   
0354   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0356   20 F5                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0358   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
0359   B7                     OR   A   
035A   C8                     RET   Z   
035B   03                     INC   BC   
035C   18 EF                  JR   skipstr   
035E                          ENDIF      
035E                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
035E                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
035E                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
035E                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
035E                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
035E                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
035E                             ; 
035E                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
035E                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
035E                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
035E                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
035E                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
035E                SKIP:        
035E                          IF   CHECKED   
035E   C5                     PUSH   BC   
035F   DD E1                  POP   IX   
0361   0B                     DEC   BC   
0362   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0363   03                     INC   BC   
0364   5F                     LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0365                          ENDIF      
0365   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0367   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0368   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0369                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INC   BC   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
0369                          ENDIF      
0369                          IF   CHECKED   
0369   B7                     OR   A   
036A   28 22                  JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
036C   03                     INC   BC   
036D                          ENDIF      
036D   FE 22                  CP   22h   
036F   CC 4D 03               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
0372   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0374   28 F1                  JR   Z,sk3   
0376   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0377   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0379   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
037B   28 EA                  JR   Z,sk3   
037D   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
037F   20 E7                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0381   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
0382                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
                              JR   sk1   
0382                          ENDIF      
0382                          IF   CHECKED   
0382   20 E4                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0384   57                     LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
0385   AB                     XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
0386   E6 06                  AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
0388   FE 02                  CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
038A   7A                     LD   A,D   
038B   C0                     RET   NZ   
038C   18 05                  JR   sk7   
038E   CB 53        SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
0390   C2 00 00               JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
0393   DD E5        SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
0395   C1                     POP   BC   
0396   3E 4E                  LD   A,"N"   
0398   C3 71 05               JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
039B                          ENDIF      
039B                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
039B   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
039D   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
039F   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
03A1   EF                     RST   28h   
03A2   E7                     RST   20h   
03A3                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
03A3                             ; Uses BC.
03A3   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
03A6   CD 11 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
03A9   7B                     LD   A,E   
03AA   F5                     PUSH   AF   
03AB   7C                     LD   A,H   
03AC   B5                     OR   L   
03AD   C4 A3 03               CALL   NZ,pdec   
03B0   F1                     POP   AF   
03B1   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
03B3   EF                     RST   28h   
03B4   C9                     RET      
03B5                             ; =============================================================================
03B5                             ;  The grave's other codes. h_grave comes here with A = the character minus
03B5                             ;  27h, not zero; the tests carry on from there. The four characters from
03B5                             ;  "+" to "." follow one another, so one range test finds them and two
03B5                             ;  rotates tell them apart.
03B5                             ; 
03B5                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader: pairs of hex digits are stored
03B5                             ;        from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is written
03B5                             ;        and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
03B5                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )   add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
03B5                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )      a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
03B5                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )   subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
03B5                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )     the address of the random seed
03B5                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )    the smaller of the two (signed)
03B5                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )    the larger
03B5                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )     the cursor off (0) or on
03B5                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )  the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
03B5                             ;    `^  ( -- )          clear the screen and home the cursor
03B5                             ;    `_  ( -- )          clear from the cursor to the end of the line
03B5                             ; 
03B5                             ;  Any other character is unsafe: the unchecked build takes it as "_", the
03B5                             ;  checked build stops with W.
03B5                             ; =============================================================================
03B5   D6 04        GRAVE2:   SUB   "+"-27h   ; "+" "," "-" "." leave 0 to 3
03B7   FE 04                  CP   4   
03B9   30 3E                  JR   NC,gv2   
03BB   1F                     RRA      ; carry: "," or "."; bit 0 of A: "-" or "."
03BC   38 13                  JR   C,gv3   
03BE                             ; `+ and `-: one routine.
03BE                          IF   CHECKED   
03BE   57                     LD   D,A   ; (the checked build tests the address first,
03BF   CD 5E 05               CALL   chkst   ;   as "!" does: the test uses A, and under
03C2   7A                     LD   A,D   ;   CP/M E too)
03C3                          ENDIF      
03C3   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
03C4   23                     INC   HL   
03C5   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
03C6   1F                     RRA      ; carry: "-"
03C7   38 02                  JR   C,gi1   
03C9   13                     INC   DE   
03CA   13                     INC   DE   
03CB   1B           GI1:      DEC   DE   
03CC   72                     LD   (HL),D   
03CD   2B                     DEC   HL   
03CE   73                     LD   (HL),E   
03CF   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; the new value is TOS
03D0   F7                     RST   30h   
03D1   1F           GV3:      RRA      ; carry: "."
03D2   38 20                  JR   C,g_seed   
03D4                             ; `, ( n -- r ). The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes
03D4                             ; every 16-bit value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones
03D4                             ; and the low ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low
03D4                             ; (XOR) before the remainder of dividing by n is taken.
03D4                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
03D4                             ; than 1.
03D4                G_RND:       
03D4                          IF   CHECKED   
03D4   2B                     DEC   HL   
03D5   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   ; n - 1 negative: n is 0 or less
03D7   23                     INC   HL   
03D8   C2 7F 05               JP   NZ,e_zero   
03DB                          ENDIF      
03DB   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = n
03DC   C5                     PUSH   BC   
03DD   2A 76 09               LD   HL,(SEED)   
03E0   44                     LD   B,H   
03E1   4D                     LD   C,L   
03E2   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
03E3   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
03E4   09                     ADD   HL,BC   ; * 5
03E5   23                     INC   HL   ; + 1
03E6   7C                     LD   A,H   
03E7   81                     ADD   A,C   
03E8   67                     LD   H,A   ; + * 256: * 261 + 1
03E9   22 76 09               LD   (SEED),HL   
03EC   AD                     XOR   L   ; (A is still the high byte)
03ED   6F                     LD   L,A   
03EE   CD 11 03               CALL   udiv   ; DE = the remainder
03F1   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
03F2   C1                     POP   BC   
03F3   F7                     RST   30h   
03F4                             ; `. pushes the address of the random seed.
03F4   E5           G_SEED:   PUSH   HL   
03F5   21 76 09               LD   HL,SEED   
03F8   F7                     RST   30h   
03F9   C6 07        GV2:      ADD   A,"+"-"$"   ; "$"
03FB   20 13                  JR   NZ,gv4   
03FD   CD A0 04     HX1:      CALL   hexc   
0400   30 0B                  JR   NC,hx2   
0402   77                     LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
0403   CD A0 04               CALL   hexc   
0406   30 05                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
0408   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
040A   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
040B   18 F0                  JR   hx1   
040D   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
040F   F7                     RST   30h   
0410   D6 18        GV4:      SUB   "<"-"$"   
0412   28 25                  JR   Z,g_min   
0414   D6 02                  SUB   ">"-"<"   
0416   28 20                  JR   Z,g_max   
0418   3D                     DEC   A   ; "?"
0419   28 30                  JR   Z,g_cur   
041B   3D                     DEC   A   ; "@"
041C   28 43                  JR   Z,g_at   
041E   D6 1E                  SUB   "^"-"@"   ; "^" leaves 0 and "_" leaves 1
0420                          IF   CHECKED   
0420   FE 02                  CP   2   
0422   D2 82 05               JP   NC,e_brack   ; anything else: W. The place is the character
0425   B7                     OR   A   
0426                          ENDIF      
0426                          IF   ANSI   
0426   20 07                  JR   NZ,ge1   
0428   CD 79 04               CALL   csi   ; "^": ESC [ H homes the cursor, and then
042B   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   ;   ESC [ J clears from there to the end of
042D   EF                     RST   28h   ;   the screen
042E   AF                     XOR   A   
042F   C6 4A        GE1:      ADD   A,"J"   ; "_": ESC [ K clears to the end of the line
0431   5F                     LD   E,A   
0432   CD 79 04               CALL   csi   
0435   7B                     LD   A,E   
0436   EF                     RST   28h   
0437   F7                     RST   30h   
0438                          ENDIF      
0438                          IF   1-ANSI   
                              JR   NZ,ge1   
                              CALL   CONCLS   
                              RST   30h   
                    GE1:      CALL   CONEOL   
                              RST   30h   
0438                          ENDIF      
0438                             ; `< and `>. The carry says which: set for the larger. The two are put in
0438                             ; order, HL the smaller and DE the larger, and then swapped for ">".
0438                             ; b < a (signed) is the borrow of b - a, turned round if the two signs
0438                             ; differ: RRA puts the borrow in bit 7, where the two XORs meet it.
0438   37           G_MAX:    SCF      ; ("<" comes in with the carry clear)
0439   D1           G_MIN:    POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
043A   F5                     PUSH   AF   
043B   7D                     LD   A,L   
043C   93                     SUB   E   
043D   7C                     LD   A,H   
043E   9A                     SBC   A,D   
043F   1F                     RRA      
0440   AC                     XOR   H   
0441   AA                     XOR   D   
0442   17                     RLA      ; carry: b < a
0443   38 01                  JR   C,gm2   
0445   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0446   F1           GM2:      POP   AF   
0447   30 01                  JR   NC,gm3   
0449   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
044A   F7           GM3:      RST   30h   
044B                          IF   ANSI   
044B                             ; `? ( flag -- ): ESC [ ? 2 5 l hides the cursor, ESC [ ? 2 5 h shows it.
044B   CD 79 04     G_CUR:    CALL   csi   
044E   3E 3F                  LD   A,"?"   
0450   EF                     RST   28h   
0451   3E 32                  LD   A,"2"   
0453   EF                     RST   28h   
0454   3E 35                  LD   A,"5"   
0456   EF                     RST   28h   
0457   7C                     LD   A,H   
0458   B5                     OR   L   
0459   3E 6C                  LD   A,"l"   
045B   28 02                  JR   Z,gc1   
045D   3E 68                  LD   A,"h"   
045F   EF           GC1:      RST   28h   
0460   DF                     RST   18h   
0461                             ; `@ ( row col -- ): ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H. (ANSI counts from 1.)
0461   D1           G_AT:     POP   DE   ; DE = the row
0462   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; (pdec uses BC)
0463   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; the column
0464   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0465   CD 79 04               CALL   csi   
0468   23                     INC   HL   
0469   CD A3 03               CALL   pdec   
046C   3E 3B                  LD   A,";"   
046E   EF                     RST   28h   
046F   E1                     POP   HL   
0470   23                     INC   HL   
0471   CD A3 03               CALL   pdec   
0474   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
0476   EF                     RST   28h   
0477   C1                     POP   BC   
0478   DF                     RST   18h   
0479                             ; csi: print ESC [, which starts every ANSI sequence. Keeps all but A.
0479   3E 1B        CSI:      LD   A,27   
047B   EF                     RST   28h   
047C   3E 5B                  LD   A,"["   
047E   EF                     RST   28h   
047F   C9                     RET      
0480                          ENDIF      
0480                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's own routines do the work (see the equates).
                    G_CUR:    LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              CALL   CONCUR   
                              RST   18h   
                    G_AT:     POP   DE   ; DE = the row, HL = the column
                              CALL   CONAT   
                              RST   18h   
0480                          ENDIF      
0480                             ; =============================================================================
0480                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
0480                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
0480                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0480                             ; =============================================================================
0480                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0480                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0480                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0480                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0480                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0480                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0480                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0480                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0480                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0480                          IF   1-TABP0   
0480                PTAB:        
0480                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
0480   AA                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
0481   B2                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
0482   C6                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
0483   BD                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
0484   A2                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
0485   45                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
0486   C3                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
0487   21                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
0488   29                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
0489   66                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
048A   3C                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
048B   ED                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
048C   34                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
048D   A4                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
048E   7A                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
048F   A0                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
0490   A9                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
0491   4D                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
0492   5C                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
0493   4E                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
0494   CC                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
0495   1C                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
0496   F8                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
0497   EB                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
0498   E7                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
0499   83                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
049A   96                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
049B   D5                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
049C   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
049D   8B                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
049E   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
049F   93                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
04A0                PTABEND:      
04A0                          ENDIF      
04A0                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
04A0                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
04A0                             ; return with the carry clear.
04A0   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
04A1   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
04A3   FE 0A                  CP   10   
04A5   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
04A7   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
04A9   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
04AB   FE 06                  CP   6   
04AD   D0                     RET   NC   
04AE   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
04B0   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
04B1   C9                     RET      
04B2                             ; =============================================================================
04B2                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
04B2                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
04B2                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
04B2                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
04B2                             ; 
04B2                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
04B2                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
04B2                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
04B2                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
04B2                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
04B2                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
04B2                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
04B2                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
04B2                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
04B2                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
04B2                             ;  data stack.
04B2                             ; =============================================================================
04B2                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
04B2                          ENDIF      
04B2                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
04B2   CD F0 04     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
04B5   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
04B6   32 7A 09               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
04B9   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
04BB   C0                     RET   NZ   
04BC                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
04BC                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
04BC                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
04BC                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
04BC   3A 7B 09     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
04BF   B7                     OR   A   
04C0   CA 6F 05     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
04C3   D5                     PUSH   DE   
04C4   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
04C7   CD F0 04     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
04CA   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
04CC   1B                     DEC   DE   
04CD   7A                     LD   A,D   
04CE   B3                     OR   E   
04CF   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
04D1   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
04D2   FE 03                  CP   3   
04D4   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
04D6   B7                     OR   A   
04D7   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
04D9   32 7A 09               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
04DC   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
04DE   B7                     OR   A   
04DF   C9                     RET      
04E0                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
04E0   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
04E1   21 7A 09               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
04E4   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
04E5   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
04E7   E1                     POP   HL   
04E8   B7                     OR   A   
04E9   C0                     RET   NZ   
04EA   CD F0 04               CALL   rawk   
04ED   C8                     RET   Z   
04EE   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
04F0                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
04F0                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
04F0                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
04F0                          ENDIF      
04F0                          IF   CHECKED   
04F0                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
04F0                          ENDIF      
04F0                          IF   CPM   
04F0   3E FF        RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
04F2                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
04F2                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
04F2   D5           PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
04F3   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04F4   5F                     LD   E,A   
04F5   3E 06                  LD   A,6   
04F7   CD FE 04               CALL   bdosx   
04FA   E1                     POP   HL   
04FB   D1                     POP   DE   
04FC   B7                     OR   A   ; (for getk)
04FD   C9                     RET      
04FE                             ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
04FE   C5           BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
04FF   D9                     EXX      
0500   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0501   D9                     EXX      
0502   4F                     LD   C,A   
0503   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0506   D9                     EXX      
0507   E1                     POP   HL   
0508   D9                     EXX      
0509   C1                     POP   BC   
050A   C9                     RET      
050B                          ENDIF      
050B                             ; =============================================================================
050B                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
050B                             ; =============================================================================
050B                          IF   CHECKED   
050B                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
050B                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
050B                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
050B                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
050B                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
050B                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
050B   EB           CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
050C   21 05 F7               LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
050F   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
0510   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0511   38 1D                  JR   C,e_under   
0513   14                     INC   D   
0514   20 16                  JR   NZ,e_over   
0516   D9                     EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
0517   7C                     LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
0518   FE 07                  CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
051A   7D                     LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
051B   D9                     EXX      
051C   20 0B                  JR   NZ,e_rover   
051E   FE E1                  CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
0520   D8                     RET   C   
0521   D9                     EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
0522   2E E0                  LD   L,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   (H is right: the pointer is in its page)
0524   D9                     EXX      
0525   3E 72                  LD   A,"r"   
0527   18 48                  JR   errp   
0529   3E 52        E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
052B   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
052C   3E 53        E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
052E   18 41                  JR   errp   
0530   31 FC 08     E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
0533   3E 73                  LD   A,"s"   
0535   18 4D                  JR   error   
0537                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
0537                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
0537                             ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
0537                             ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
0537   04           E_HI:     INC   B   
0538   10 42                  DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
053A   CF                     RST   08h   
053B   42                     LD   B,D   
053C   4B                     LD   C,E   
053D   3E 55                  LD   A,"U"   
053F   18 43                  JR   error   
0541                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
0541                             ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
0541                             ; program's end.
0541                CHKHP:       
0541                          ENDIF      
0541                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0541                             ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
0541                             ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
0541                             ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
0541   1F                     RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
0542   C6 40                  ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
0544   87                     ADD   A,A   
0545   38 10                  JR   C,e_heap   
0547   3A 07 00               LD   A,(0007h)   
054A   3D                     DEC   A   
054B   BC                     CP   H   
054C   38 09                  JR   C,e_heap   
054E                          ENDIF      
054E                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
054E                          ENDIF      
054E                          IF   CHECKED   
054E   D5                     PUSH   DE   
054F   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0550   2A 38 09               LD   HL,(NPEND)   
0553   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0554   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0555   D1                     POP   DE   
0556   D8                     RET   C   
0557   B7           E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
0558   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
055A   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
055C   18 13                  JR   errp   
055E                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
055E                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
055E                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
055E                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
055E                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
055E                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
055E                             ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
055E   23           CHKST:    INC   HL   
055F   7C                     LD   A,H   
0560   2B                     DEC   HL   
0561   FE 09                  CP   LETPAGE   
0563   38 07                  JR   C,e_store   
0565                          ENDIF      
0565                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
0565                          ENDIF      
0565                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0565   5F                     LD   E,A   
0566   3A 07 00               LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
0569   3D                     DEC   A   
056A   BB                     CP   E   
056B   D0                     RET   NC   
056C                          ENDIF      
056C                          IF   CHECKED   
056C                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
056C                             ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
056C   3E 4F        E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
056E   11                     DB   11h   
056F   3E 42        E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
0571                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
0571   D1           ERRP:     POP   DE   
0572   18 10                  JR   error   
0574   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop prstr's return
0575   E1                     POP   HL   ;   address, put the string's address back in
0576   11                     DB   11h   ;   TOS, and step over the next two bytes: Q
0577   44           E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
0578   4D                     LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
0579   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
057B   11                     DB   11h   
057C   3E 58        E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
057E   11                     DB   11h   
057F   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
0581   11                     DB   11h   
0582   3E 57        E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
0584                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
0584                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
0584                             ; 
0584                             ;   Err X @ line,col
0584                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
0584                             ;   Rtn n
0584   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
0585   5F                     LD   E,A   
0586   CD 3B 06               CALL   pnl   
0589   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
058E   7B                     LD   A,E   
058F   EF                     RST   28h   
0590   CD 41 06               CALL   pmsg   
0593   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
0597   0B                     DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
0598                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
0598                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
0598                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
0598   21 80 09               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
059B   11 00 00               LD   DE,0   
059E   78                     LD   A,B   
059F   FE 0A                  CP   PROG/256   
05A1   38 14                  JR   C,er3   
05A3   24                     INC   H   
05A4   6B                     LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
05A5   13           ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
05A6   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05A7   7D           ER2:      LD   A,L   
05A8   91                     SUB   C   
05A9   7C                     LD   A,H   
05AA   98                     SBC   A,B   
05AB   30 09                  JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
05AD   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
05AE   23                     INC   HL   
05AF   FE 0A                  CP   10   
05B1   20 F4                  JR   NZ,er2   
05B3   F1                     POP   AF   
05B4   18 EF                  JR   er1   
05B6   E1           ER2X:     POP   HL   
05B7   C5           ER3:      PUSH   BC   
05B8   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05B9   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05BA   CD A3 03               CALL   pdec   ; the line
05BD   3E 2C                  LD   A,","   
05BF   EF                     RST   28h   
05C0   D1                     POP   DE   
05C1   E1                     POP   HL   
05C2   B7                     OR   A   
05C3   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
05C5   23                     INC   HL   
05C6   CD A3 03               CALL   pdec   ; the column
05C9                             ; The two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
05C9                             ;                       Rtn n
05C9                             ; TOS is in memory with the rest (pushed).
05C9   CD 3B 06               CALL   pnl   
05CC   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
05D1   21 06 F7               LD   HL,(2-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; SP - (DSTOP-2) is minus twice the
05D4   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ;   depth (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed
05D5   E7                     RST   20h   ;   with the first value and holds nothing)
05D6   CD 1D 06               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
05D9   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
05DB   EF                     RST   28h   
05DC   79                     LD   A,C   
05DD   FE 09                  CP   9   
05DF   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
05E1   CD 41 06               CALL   pmsg   
05E4   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
05E9   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
05EB   60           ER6:      LD   H,B   ; C = the number of cells to show (B is 0:
05EC                             ;   phalf left the depth in BC)
05EC   69                     LD   L,C   
05ED   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
05EE   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
05EF   0C                     INC   C   
05F0   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
05F1   28 11                  JR   Z,er8   
05F3   2B                     DEC   HL   
05F4   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
05F5   2B                     DEC   HL   
05F6   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
05F7   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05F8   C5                     PUSH   BC   
05F9   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
05FB   EF                     RST   28h   
05FC   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05FD   CD 9B 03               CALL   psgn   
0600   C1                     POP   BC   
0601   E1                     POP   HL   
0602   18 EC                  JR   er7   
0604   CD 3B 06     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
0607   52 74 6E 20 22         DB   "Rtn ",22h   
060C   D9                     EXX      ; twice the depth is RSTOP less the pointer:
060D   3E E0                  LD   A,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   the low bytes are enough, since even an
060F   95                     SUB   L   ;   overflowing stack holds under 128 entries
0610   D9                     EXX      
0611   6F                     LD   L,A   
0612   60                     LD   H,B   ; (B is still 0)
0613   CD 1D 06               CALL   phalf   
0616   CD 3B 06               CALL   pnl   
0619   22                     DB   22h   
061A                          ENDIF      
061A                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
061A   C3 15 01               JP   endprog   
061D                          ENDIF      
061D                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
061D                          ENDIF      
061D                          IF   CHECKED   
061D                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C.
061D   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
061F   CB 1D                  RR   L   
0621   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0622   CD A3 03               CALL   pdec   
0625   C1                     POP   BC   
0626   C9                     RET      
0627                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0627                             ; "$", and the texts of the report). A
0627                             ; NUL first is an error: Q.
0627   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
0628   23                     INC   HL   
0629   FE 22                  CP   22h   
062B   C8                     RET   Z   
062C   B7                     OR   A   
062D   CA 74 05               JP   Z,e_dollar   
0630   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0632   20 04                  JR   NZ,prs1   
0634   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0635   23                     INC   HL   
0636   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
0638   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
0639   18 EC                  JR   prstr   
063B                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
063B                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
063B   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
063D   EF                     RST   28h   
063E   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0640   EF                     RST   28h   
0641   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
0642   CD 27 06               CALL   prstr   
0645   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
0646   C9                     RET      
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                             ; =============================================================================
0647                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
0647                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
0647                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
0647                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
0647                             ;    n         take line n out
0647                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
0647                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;    ^G        run the program
0647                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
0647                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
0647                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
0647                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
0647                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
0647                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
0647                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
0647                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
0647                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
0647                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
0647                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
0647                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
0647                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
0647                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
0647                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
0647                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
0647                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
0647                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
0647                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  Things to know:
0647                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
0647                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
0647                             ;      after editing it.
0647                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
0647                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
0647                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
0647                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
0647                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
0647                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
0647                             ; 
0647                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
0647                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
0647                             ; =============================================================================
0647                          IF   EDGEN   
                    INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDGEN   
                              JR   edit0   
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDITOR   
                                 ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
                    RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   lf1   
                                 ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
                                 ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
                                 ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
                    ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
                    ES1:      CALL   rawk   
                              JR   NZ,es2   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,B   
                              OR   C   
                              JR   NZ,es1   
                              CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
                              JR   edit   
                    ES2:      CP   "["   
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
                    ES3:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   40h   
                              JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
                              SUB   "C"   
                              JR   Z,right   
                              DEC   A   ; "D"?
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
                                 ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
                    LEFT:     LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                    LF1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
                                 ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
                                 ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
                    EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
                              DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
                    SKEND:    POP   DE   
                    EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
                                 ; edit: start a new input line.
                    EDIT:     EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,0   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
                              LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
                    ED1:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
                              CP   " "   
                              JR   NC,insc   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,bsp   
                              CP   2   
                              JR   Z,left   ; ^B
                              CP   6   
                              JR   Z,right   ; ^F
                              CP   1Bh   
                              JR   Z,esc   
                              PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
                              LD   HL,cmds   
                              LD   B,NCMD   
                    ED2:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,ed3   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   ed2   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
                    ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   H,(HL)   
                              LD   L,A   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
                                 ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
                                 ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
                    FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
                              LD   L,E   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              DEC   L   
                              CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              LD   BC,LINEBUF   
                              RET      
                                 ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
                                 ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
                                 ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
                    BSP:      LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    BS1:      INC   L   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,bs1   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   D,E   
                              DEC   E   
                              JR   ic2   
                                 ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
                                 ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
                    INSC:     LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
                              LD   A,B   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (HL),B   
                              LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              INC   L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,ic1   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   L   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   D,E   
                    IC2:      CALL   tail   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
                                 ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
                    TAIL:     LD   C,L   
                    TA1:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ta2   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   ta1   
                    TA2:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   C   
                              RET   Z   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              DEC   L   
                              JR   ta2   
                                 ; ekey: wait for a key
                    EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,ekey   
                              RET      
                                 ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
                    CMDS:     DB   13   
                              DW   cret   
                              DB   7   ; ^G
                              DW   crun   
                              DB   12   ; ^L
                              DW   clist   
                              DB   5   ; ^E
                              DW   cedln   
                              DB   18   ; ^R
                              DW   cread   
                              DB   23   ; ^W
                              DW   cwrite   
                              DB   14   ; ^N
                              DW   cnew   
                              DB   24   ; ^X
                              DW   LEAVE   
                    NCMD:     EQU   8   
                                 ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
                    CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
                              CP   14   
                              JR   NZ,ged0   
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   (PROG),A   
                    GED0:     JR   gedit   
                                 ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
                                 ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
                    CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; (no such line: `edit` clears it again)
                              CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged0   
                              LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                    CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   ; copy it, and show it, up to its CR (or LF)
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
                              JR   NZ,ce1   
                    CE2:      EX   DE,HL   ; the cursor is at the line's end
                              LD   E,L   
                              JP   ed1   
                                 ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
                                 ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
                                 ; and anything else is run where it is.
                    CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   HL,(EDLN)   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   Z,cr1   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   delln   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ins   
                    CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
                              LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
                              ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
                              JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,cr2   
                              POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
                              CALL   delln   
                              JR   gedit   
                    CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
                                 ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
                                 ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
                    INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
                              POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   A,E   
                              SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
                              PUSH   BC   ; the text
                              LD   C,A   
                              LD   B,0   
                              PUSH   BC   ; its length
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
                              CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
                              SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
                              LD   B,H   
                              LD   C,L   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
                              PUSH   HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
                              POP   BC   ; the length
                              POP   DE   ; where it goes
                              POP   HL   ; the text
                              LDIR      
                    GEDIT:    JP   edit   
                                 ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
                    CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
                              DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
                    ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
                                 ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
                    ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
                              LD   (HEAP),HL   
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDITOR   
                              POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
                                 ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
                    CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   NZ,li0   
                              INC   L   ;   then from line 1
                    LI0:      PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   
                              POP   DE   
                    LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
                              CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
                              CP   3   
                              CALL   NZ,ekey   ; any key but Ctrl-C: wait for one more
                              CP   3   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C, first or second, ends the list
                    LI3:      PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   ;   a space,
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              CALL   prl   ;   and the line
                              JR   li1   
                                 ; delln: take line n (in HL) out: copy everything after it down over it.
                    DELLN:    CALL   find   
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   
                              CALL   nxl   ; HL -> the next line
                    DE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   NZ,de1   
                              RET      
                                 ; find: HL = a line number. Returns HL -> that line, or -> the NUL at the end
                                 ; of the text if there are fewer lines (or the number is 0). Keeps BC.
                    FIND:     EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                    FI1:      DEC   DE   
                              LD   A,D   
                              OR   E   
                              RET   Z   
                              CALL   nxl   
                              JR   NZ,fi1   
                              RET      
                                 ; nxl: step HL over one line, to just past its LF (and return not-zero), or
                                 ; stop at the NUL that ends the text (and return zero).
                    NXL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,nxl   
                              OR   A   
                              RET      
                                 ; prl: print the line at HL, to its LF; HL -> just past it.
                    PRL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,prl   
                              RET      
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDGEN   
                                 ; ^R, generic: what comes in from now until ^Z is the program. A CR is
                                 ; stored as CR LF; a LF right after a line end is dropped (it is the CR's
                                 ; own, or an empty line's), and a LF anywhere else ends a line too. A last
                                 ; line with no end is given one. Nothing is echoed, and there is no check
                                 ; for running out of memory.
                    CREAD:    LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; (as if a line had just ended: the byte is
                              INC   HL   ;   the line buffer's last, and spare)
                    RD1:      CALL   ekey   
                              LD   C,A   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd2   
                              LD   A,10   ; ^Z ends the last line, as a LF would
                    RD2:      CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,rd3   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,rd4   ; straight after a line end: dropped
                              LD   A,13   ; anywhere else it ends the line
                    RD3:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,rd4   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; after a CR goes a LF
                              INC   HL   
                    RD4:      LD   A,C   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd1   
                              LD   (HL),0   
                    GED1:     JP   edit   
                                 ; ^W, generic: the text is printed as it is, for the terminal to capture.
                    CWRITE:   LD   HL,PROG   
                    CW1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged1   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   cw1   
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    CFCB:     EQU   005Ch   ; the file's name is kept here, where the CCP
                                 ;   put the one from the command line
                                 ; ^W, CP/M: write the file: delete the old one, make it anew, write the
                                 ; text in records of 128 bytes, and close it. The text's NUL and the 127
                                 ; bytes after it are set to ^Z meanwhile, which pads the last record. (A
                                 ; full disk or directory is not noticed: the calls fail and that is all.)
                    CWRITE:   CALL   setname   
                              LD   C,19   ; delete
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   C,22   ; make
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    CW1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,cw1   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   B,128   
                    CW2:      LD   (HL),1Ah   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   cw2   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    CW3:      LD   A,E   ; a record that starts before the end is written
                              SUB   L   
                              LD   A,D   
                              SBC   A,H   
                              JR   NC,cw4   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   C,21   ; write, from where the record lies
                              CALL   frec   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   cw3   
                    CW4:      LD   (HL),0   ; the NUL again
                              LD   C,16   ; close,
                              LD   HL,edit   ;   and from there back to the editor
                              PUSH   HL   
                                 ; fbdos: BDOS function C on the file. (^W ends by running on into it.)
                    FBDOS:    LD   DE,CFCB   
                              JP   BDOS   
                                 ; frec: BDOS function C (read or write a record) with the 128 bytes at DE.
                                 ; Returns A = the BDOS's answer, HL = DE and DE = DE + 128.
                    FREC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   BC   
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   HL,128   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              RET      
                                 ; setname: if a name was typed (the line does not start with its CR), put it
                                 ; in the FCB: up to 8 characters, a dot, up to 3 more, in capitals. The drive
                                 ; is the current one. Then, name or no name, clear the FCB after the name,
                                 ; as it must be before a file is opened or made.
                    SETNAME:   LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                              LD   A,(DE)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              LD   HL,CFCB   
                              LD   (HL),0   ; the current drive
                              LD   B,11   
                    SN1:      INC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              DJNZ   sn1   
                              LD   L,CFCB+1   
                    SN2:      LD   A,(DE)   
                              INC   DE   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              CP   "."   
                              JR   NZ,sn3   
                              LD   L,CFCB+9   ; the type
                              JR   sn2   
                    SN3:      CP   "a"   
                              JR   C,sn4   
                              AND   5Fh   ; a capital
                    SN4:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   sn2   
                    FCBCLR:   LD   HL,CFCB+12   
                              LD   B,24   
                    FC1:      LD   (HL),0   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   fc1   
                              RET      
                                 ; ^R, CP/M: read the file. A name typed before the key is the file's name
                                 ; from now on. It runs on into load, which returns to the editor.
                    CREAD:    CALL   setname   
                              LD   HL,edit   
                              PUSH   HL   
                                 ; load: read the file into PROG. No such file: no program. The text ends at
                                 ; the file"s first ^Z (1Ah), which pads a text file"s last record; one more
                                 ; goes after the last record, so the search always stops. And every line
                                 ; must end in LF: a last line without one is given a CR LF. (The FCB is
                                 ; clear after its name: the CCP left it so, or setname did.)
                    LOAD:     LD   C,15   ; open (no such file: the first read fails
                              CALL   fbdos   ;   too)
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    LD1:      LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
                              CALL   frec   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ld1   
                              LD   (HL),1Ah   ; (HL = where the record that failed would be)
                              LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   A,10   ; (a file with no text needs nothing added)
                    TR1:      INC   HL   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the character before this one
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,tr1   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,tr2   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              INC   HL   
                    TR2:      LD   (HL),0   
                              RET      
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                             ; =============================================================================
0647                          IF   CPM   
0647                             ; The RAM pages follow the image; the heap may grow to the BDOS.
0647                START:       
0647                          ENDIF      
0647                          IF   CPM*CHECKED   
0647                             ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at
0647                             ; 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is
0647                             ; caught at (see e_hi: the byte there is CP/M's JP, C3h), and no key
0647                             ; is held back.
0647   21 00 09               LD   HL,LET   
064A   AF                     XOR   A   
064B   77           INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
064C   2C                     INC   L   
064D   F2 4B 06               JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0650                          ENDIF      
0650                          IF   CPM   
0650   21 08 01               LD   HL,vecs   ; the RST routines go down into page zero
0653   11 08 00               LD   DE,0008h   
0656   01 2C 00               LD   BC,vecend-vecs   
0659   ED B0                  LDIR      
065B                          ENDIF      
065B                          IF   CPM*EDITOR   
                              CALL   load   ; the file named on the command line
                              JP   edit0   
065B                          ENDIF      
065B                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
065B   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   ; open the file named on the command line
065E   0E 0F                  LD   C,15   ; (no such file: the first read fails too,
0660   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   ;   and the program is empty)
0663   11 00 0A               LD   DE,PROG   
0666   D5           LD1:      PUSH   DE   
0667   0E 1A                  LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
0669   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
066C   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   
066F   0E 14                  LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
0671   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0674   E1                     POP   HL   ; HL = the address this record went to
0675   B7                     OR   A   
0676   20 07                  JR   NZ,ld2   
0678   11 80 00               LD   DE,128   
067B   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
067C   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
067D   18 E7                  JR   ld1   
067F   36 00        LD2:      LD   (HL),0   ; the end of the file counts as NUL
0681   23                     INC   HL   ; the heap starts after it
0682   01 00 0A               LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0685   C3 76 01               JP   st2   
0688                          ENDIF      
0688                          IF   CPM   
0688                             ; RAM pages, after the image
0688                RSPAGE:   EQU   (imgend + 255) / 256   
0688                DSPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 1   
0688                LETPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 2   
0688                PROG:     EQU   LETPAGE*256 + 256   
0688                          ENDIF      
0688                IMGEND:      


